\section{What is refused}{

Each of the following is one row of the unconvertible report (question
code, item, reason), and all of them are listed at once:
\itemize{
\item a question whose type is not authorable -- the eight deferred LimeSurvey
types (\code{P}, \code{H}, \code{1}, \verb{;}, \code{:}, \code{*}, \code{|}, \code{I}) and any unknown one;
\item a question code that is not a spec code, or a duplicate of an earlier one;
\item a question or option with no wording in the base language, or a shape the
\code{\link[=lss_spec]{lss_spec()}} validator refuses (too few options, an array without rows or
columns, a cap larger than the option list);
\item a display condition in any other form than the three above -- a
hand-written equation is never guessed at;
\item a quota combining several questions, built on a question the spec cannot
target, or carrying an action other than "terminate";
\item a group with no title in the base language (its questions go with it),
and a question belonging to no group at all;
\item a question storing rows on a second answer scale, or in a section its
type does not carry: the shape on file is not the shape lssdoc emits,
and half an option list is not a smaller option list;
\item a structural column carrying something a specification has no field for
and \code{\link[=write_lss]{write_lss()}} would silently replace by its own constant, where that
changes what the respondent meets: a group display equation
(\code{groups.grelevance}) or randomization, a per-subquestion relevance (an
array filter), a validation regex (\code{preg}), per-question JavaScript
(\code{question_l10ns.script}), encrypted storage (\code{encrypted}). The columns
that change nothing a respondent sees -- assessment values,
\code{same_default}, \code{modulename}, \code{same_script}, a quota URL description --
are noted in the lossy warning instead;
\item a multilingual survey that does not declare its base language: a
specification's first language IS its base language, and \verb{<languages>}
lists the base one last.
}
